Sur les raisons d’éviter les global assignements, comme le disait également
Joel, on peut se référer au R inferno, p. 36
http://www.burns-stat.com/pages/Tutor/R_inferno.pdf:

it is expected in R that a function has no side effects. A function that
makes a global assignment violates this expectation. To users unfamiliar
with the code (and even to the writer of the code after a few weeks) there
will be an object that changes seemingly by magic.

